#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_diagonal_matrix

#% text
# `is_diagonal_matrix(m)` is true when every entry of `m` off the main diagonal is zero; `is_diagonal_matrix(m, k)` when every entry off the `k`-th diagonal is.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The matrix need not be square.

#% item
# The result is false for anything that is not a matrix.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_diagonal_matrix([[1, 0], [0, 2]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_diagonal_matrix([[1, 1], [0, 2]])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_diagonal_matrix([[0, 1], [0, 0]], 1)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_diagonal_matrix(diagonal_matrix([1, 2, 3]))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_upper_triangular_matrix`, `is_lower_triangular_matrix`, `diagonal_matrix`
